# `j % u` in the inner of two loops; u is shown in front of them to be an int32 of at least one, j lies in [0, 999]. A division holds every turn at six cycles. For a dividend of at most 32 bits that is not negative and such a
# divisor the remainder is exact by two multiplications (Lemire, Kaser, Kurz 2019): c = floor((2^64 - 1) / u) + 1 . j % u = the high half of ((c * j mod 2^64) * u). c hangs on u alone: it is made once, in front of BOTH loops.
# function run(u: number) { const a = new Int32Array(100); for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) for (let j = 0; j < 1000; j++) a[i] = a[i] + j % u; return a[7]; }
